            <ArticleTitle>Nickel-Catalyzed Synthesis of Stereochemically Defined Enamides via Bi- and Tricomponent Coupling Reaction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5034-5037</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02166</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The stereoselective synthesis of (E)-trisubstituted tertiary enamides is documented via site-selective Ni-catalyzed β-arylation of allenamides with boronic acids in high yields (up to 89%). The nucleophilic character of the &quot;organo-Ni&quot; intermediates is further exploited to implement a one-pot tricomponent procedure involving the final allylation of aldehydes (yields up to 93%). Mechanistic insights and efficiency on a gram scale process were also documented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
